The clinical pattern is classic for herpes zoster: neuropathic burning precedes a unilateral dermatomal eruption. At about one week, with lesions already crusted, antivirals are generally too late to provide meaningful benefit; zoster at age 26 should raise concern for unrecognized immunodeficiency, making HIV screening the best choice here. I’ll record this conclusion before finalizing.

